  "system": {
    "group": "HreoEGHHF8fvUBHd",
    "headers": {
      "concept": "FIRSTLIGHT tactical team operator, former ATF agent: the one who's already seen it",
      "chronicle": "The Ward File",
      "ambition": "Find whatever took Ortiz.",
      "desire": "For someone else on the team to see what she saw and not break.",
      "touchstones": "<h3>Touchstones</h3><ul><li>Ortiz&#39;s widow, in Tucson. Navarro sends her money every month without telling her why.</li></ul>",
      "sire": "",
      "generation": "",
      "creedfields": "Any direct conflict (physical, social or mental) with the supernatural during the Hunt.",
      "cellname": "Puget Cell"
    },
    "bio": {
      "age": {
        "trueage": "38",
        "apparent": ""
      },
      "dateof": {
        "birth": "",
        "death": ""
      },
      "history": ""
    },
    "biography": "<table class=\"sbn-ficha\"><tbody><tr><th>Concept</th><td>FIRSTLIGHT tactical team operator, former ATF agent: the one who&#39;s already seen it</td></tr><tr><th>Age</th><td>38</td></tr><tr><th>Ambition</th><td>Find whatever took Ortiz.</td></tr><tr><th>Desire</th><td>For someone else on the team to see what she saw and not break.</td></tr><tr><th>Dice pools</th><td>Physical 6 · Social 2 · Mental 4 · Firearms 7 · Athletics 5 · Awareness 5 · Brawl 5</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Demeanor</h3><p>Thirty-eight, dark-haired, hair in a short braid. Wears a Saint Michael medal that isn&#39;t hers. Always on point, with the flashlight.</p><p>One of the six operators of @UUID[Actor.abaWg7NwNQvM0sDc]{FIRSTLIGHT Tactical Team}. She&#39;s the only one on the team who&#39;s seen a creature up close, and the others know it even if they don&#39;t ask.</p><h3>Hunter</h3><table class=\"sbn-ficha\"><tbody><tr><th>Cell</th><td>@UUID[JournalEntry.dnsWkdXVJ19riBLa.JournalEntryPage.O8yPSIYLlTrKHm8G]{Puget Cell}</td></tr><tr><th>Creed</th><td>Faithful. <em>Desperation:</em> Any direct conflict (physical, social or mental) with the supernatural during the Hunt.</td></tr><tr><th>Drive</th><td>Vengeance. <em>Redemption:</em> She finds redemption when the Cell destroys a creature that killed an innocent, and she&#39;s there to see it.</td></tr><tr><th>Edges</th><td>Repel the Unnatural (One Step Back)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Tucson, 2021. A warehouse search. Her partner, Ortiz, went in first. What came out of the dark wasn&#39;t a person, and it took him. Nobody believed her, except a man from the Department of Homeland Security who was waiting for her outside the hospital.</p><p>@UUID[JournalEntry.LfywH6qtS3GxDxJx.JournalEntryPage.6EUQdXXmzOvNtRy0]{Pregen: Teresa “Tess” Navarro · Operator}</p>",
    "appearance": "<p>Thirty-eight, dark-haired, hair in a short braid. Wears a Saint Michael medal that isn&#39;t hers. Always on point, with the flashlight.</p>",
    "equipment": "",
    "notes": "",
    "privatenotes": "<h3>Proposed (not in the docs)</h3><ul><li>The whole character is proposed (SPEC §6.2: three named operators on the tactical team). Conversion of the @UUID[Actor.abaWg7NwNQvM0sDc]{FIRSTLIGHT Tactical Team} pools (Physical 6, Social 2, Mental 4; Firearms 7, Athletics 5, Awareness 5, Brawl 5; Health 7, Willpower 5) to Attributes and Skills: Dexterity 3 + Firearms 4, Dexterity 3 + Athletics 2, Strength 3 + Brawl 2, Wits 3 + Awareness 2; Health = Stamina 4 + 3; Willpower = Composure 3 + Resolve 2. Investigation, Occult, Intimidation, and Drive are her own.</li><li>Faithful Creed, Vengeance Drive, Repel the Unnatural Edge (the medal) with the “One Step Back” Perk.</li><li>The doc says most of the team has never seen it: Navarro is the exception.</li></ul>",
